jobs.description:
The chief information officer (CIO) is the highest-level person in charge of information technology and information management in an enterprise. He is responsible for formulating enterprise IT strategy, information systems, digital infrastructure, data management and technical operation planning.
The core task of this position is to ensure that enterprise information systems can support business strategies while improving organizational operational efficiency, information security, data utilization capabilities and digitalization levels.

Core responsibilities

1. IT strategic planning
- Formulate the enterprise's medium and long-term IT strategy and technology development route;
- Ensure IT strategy is aligned with the overall business objectives of the enterprise;
- Develop annual IT plans, budgets and investment priorities;
- Evaluate the application value of new technologies to corporate business;
- Provide IT strategic advice to CEO, Board of Directors and senior management.

2. Enterprise information system management
- Fully responsible for the core information system of the enterprise;
- Manage ERP, CRM, HRIS, data platforms and enterprise applications;
- Promote the integration and modernization of information systems;
- Ensure stable and efficient operation of the system;
- Establish enterprise-level IT architecture and management standards.

3. Digital transformation
- Develop an enterprise digital transformation roadmap;
- Promote the digitization and automation of business processes;
- Lead large-scale digital transformation projects;
- Evaluate the application of AI, cloud computing and automation technologies;
- Improve the overall digital operation capabilities of the enterprise.

4. IT operations and services
- Oversee corporate IT infrastructure and day-to-day operations;
- Establish IT service management system;
- Optimize IT service quality and response efficiency;
- Manage technology suppliers and external service providers;
- Establish IT service level and performance management mechanisms.

5. Information Security and Risks
- Collaborate with CISO and security team to establish information security system;
- Supervise corporate information system security risks;
- Establish disaster recovery and business continuity mechanisms;
- Manage major IT risks and system incidents;
- Ensure that enterprise information systems comply with internal governance requirements.

6. Data and information management
- Develop enterprise data management strategy;
- Promote the construction of data governance, data quality and data standards;
- Establish enterprise-level data architecture;
- Improve data accessibility and analysis capabilities;
- Use data to support business decisions.

7. Technology budget and resource management
- Develop annual IT budget;
- Manage technical personnel, systems, infrastructure and supplier resources;
- Optimize IT cost structure;
- Evaluate return on technology investment;
- Properly allocate technical resources according to business priorities.

8. Team and organization building
- Lead the enterprise IT organization;
- Manage IT Directors, Technology Operations Leaders, Enterprise Architecture and other teams;
- Establish an IT talent training and succession system;
- Promote the professional development of the technical team;
- Establish an IT culture that is service-oriented to the business.

Qualifications

Educational background
- Bachelor degree or above in computer science, information systems, information technology, engineering, business administration or related majors;
- MBA, Information Systems Management or related master's degree preferred.

work experience
- More than 20 years of experience in IT, information systems or enterprise technology management;
- More than 15 years of senior IT management experience;
- Experience in senior positions such as CIO, VP of IT, SVP of Information Technology or IT Director is preferred;
- Experience in large enterprise information system management;
- Experience in IT management of global, multi-regional or complex organizations is preferred.

core competencies
- Enterprise IT strategy;
- Information system management;
- Digital transformation;
- IT service management;
- Enterprise architecture;
- Data governance;
- Cloud computing;
-IT risk management;
- Supplier management;
- IT budget management;
- Organizational leadership;
- Senior management communication.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
- IT system availability;
- IT service SLA achievement rate;
- Digital project completion rate;
- On-time delivery rate of IT projects;
- IT operating cost optimization rate;
- IT user satisfaction;
- System failure and recovery time;
- Digital process coverage;
- IT ROI;
- Data quality and governance achievement rate.

